From: valisolaris <valisolaris@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 18:42:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] windows-port: add a failing regression test for
 paste-burst fragmentation

crossterm's Windows event source emits a matching KeyEventKind::Release
for every Press, including for clipboard-injected paste characters.
read_input_batch's paste-burst coalescing didn't know about this: the
release right after the very first pasted character ended the burst
after one key, so a paste never coalesced into a single Event::Paste
and an embedded Enter reached the shell as a literal, premature submit.

This commit only extracts the burst-continuation decision into a pure
classify_burst_event() function (no behavior change) and adds tests,
including one that reproduces the fragmentation with a synthetic
Press/Release-interleaved event stream. It fails as expected; the fix
follows in the next commit.
